The run reports all six primary configurations (ERC and LSTM, each baseline/regime/blend) plus equal_weight. The primary LSTM parameters are trained on the initial estimation window and remain fixed during the walk-forward evaluation, while the HMM, predictive-density models, and state covariance estimates are refit on their scheduled expanding-window cadence. The 2015-2018 period is used for development and specification selection. The 2019-2026 results are non-anticipative historical walk-forward evidence but are not an independent holdout because that period was previously inspected. real_data_summary.csv reports gross performance. Net-of-cost results under the 5, 10, and 25 basis-point assumptions are reported in real_data_cost_sensitivity.csv; DSR is reported separately above.
